 "era.cockpit.records": {
  "title": "Cockpit page: Records (sambarentals.com/payouts)",
  "audience": [
   "era",
   "system"
  ],
  "text": "The paper trail. Every scheduled visit at every villa, newest first: routine cleans, turnovers, pre-arrival preparations, deep cleans and inspection rounds — done, skipped, not confirmed, or never sent — with the photos the housekeeper sent and what happened to the visit step by step. Photos are kept permanently.\n\n### Finding something\n\n• Pick the villa and the month at the top. Visits , Handovers and Inspections narrow by kind; Needs a look shows what Maya flagged, rounds that raised repairs, and visits that were not confirmed or never sent.\n\n• To check the state of a unit on a date: pick the villa, find the visit before and after that date, open the photos. The What happened list on each visit shows when it was sent, tapped, moved, chased and closed.\n\n• Tap a record: the photos, what Maya flagged, what the housekeeper wrote, what was running low, and which repairs came out of it.\n\n• Each record says which guest it sits before or after , so a damage claim can be answered with the photo taken before that guest arrived and the one taken after they left.\n\n• Share as PDF makes a link to the record as a PDF with all its photos. Anyone with the link can open it without logging in; forward it to an owner or attach it to a claim.\n\nNothing is added here by hand. A visit with no photos is still a record: Done means the housekeeper said so, Not confirmed means nobody did, Uncovered means there was nobody to send it to."
 },
